{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Rbn7VUfYeJBftKNkfzLQRT","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"CoRL 2024 instruction for reviews reviewer form scoring scale\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"CoRL 2024 - Instruction for Reviews\",\"url\":\"https://2024.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-reviews\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2024 - Instruction for Authors\",\"url\":\"https://2024.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-authors\"},{\"title\":\"Reviewers in 2024\",\"url\":\"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC12056528/\"},{\"title\":\"Reviewer Guidelines — CoRL 2023\",\"url\":\"https://www.corl2023.org/reviewer-guidelines\"},{\"title\":\"CoRL 2024 - Papers XX\",\"url\":\"https://2024.corl.org/program/papers-xx\"},{\"title\":\"Reviewers in 2024\",\"url\":\"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC12055280/\"},{\"title\":\"Reviewers in 2024\",\"url\":\"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC12056555/\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found the CoRL 2024 Instructions for Reviews page. Here's what I found:\n\nSubmissions will be evaluated based on the significance and novelty of the results, either theoretical or empirical, with results judged on the degree to which they have been objectively established and/or their potential for scientific and technological impact, as well as their relevance to robotic learning.\n\nHowever, the search results from the official CoRL 2024 Instructions for Reviews page don't contain specific details about the reviewer form scoring scale. The content provided focuses on review criteria and the review process, but doesn't include the actual scoring scale metrics that would be used by reviewers when completing their review forms.\n\nTo get the complete information about the specific scoring scale, you may need to visit the full instructions page directly at https://2024.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-reviews, as the search results appear to have captured only a portion of that page's content.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a551ef02-7e02-4516-a695-4e220ef1b867","uuid":"81286cdf-1e9d-470e-a8d3-ad2539eba119","timestamp":"2026-05-27T03:32:30.772Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"CoRL 2024 instruction for reviews reviewer form scoring scale","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_018MxY4UaZfmUwHPKNoWdsnq","content":[{"title":"CoRL 2024 - Instruction for Reviews","url":"https://2024.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-reviews"},{"title":"CoRL 2024 - Instruction for Authors","url":"https://2024.corl.org/contributions/instruction-for-authors"},{"title":"Reviewers in 2024","url":"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC12056528/"},{"title":"Reviewer Guidelines — CoRL 2023","url":"https://www.corl2023.org/reviewer-guidelines"},{"title":"CoRL 2024 - Papers XX","url":"https://2024.corl.org/program/papers-xx"},{"title":"Reviewers in 2024","url":"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC12055280/"},{"title":"Reviewers in 2024","url":"https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/pmc/articles/PMC12056555/"}]},"Based on the search results, I found the CoRL 2024 Instructions for Reviews page. Here's what I found:\n\nSubmissions will be evaluated based on the significance and novelty of the results, either theoretical or empirical, with results judged on the degree to which they have been objectively established and/or their potential for scientific and technological impact, as well as their relevance to robotic learning.\n\nHowever, the search results from the official CoRL 2024 Instructions for Reviews page don't contain specific details about the reviewer form scoring scale. The content provided focuses on review criteria and the review process, but doesn't include the actual scoring scale metrics that would be used by reviewers when completing their review forms.\n\nTo get the complete information about the specific scoring scale,