ut VLA training. Training reduces heads in TracVLA.\n4. **Metric dependence**: CKA reverses RSA ordering for trained vs untrained representations.\n\n## Experimental Design Reference (from review_context.yaml)\nThe paper covers these experiment plans:\n- plan_001: SigLIP+Projector RSA (OpenVLA only)\n- plan_002: DINO baseline RSA (R²=0.687 without language/action training)\n- plan_003: Per-layer RSA degradation curve (inverted-U, OpenVLA only, CKA reversal)\n- plan_004: Output head analysis (cos_sim=1.0, trivial verification of frozen encoder)\n- plan_005: 6 probing methods × 2 benchmarks (trained≈untrained, CKA reversal breaks consistency)\n- plan_006: Instruction ablation (Δ=0.004, structurally guaranteed null)\n- plan_007: 2×2 matrix (all conditions converge to 0.48-0.49, expected null)\n- plan_008: Random instruction control (max Δ=0.017, guaranteed by causal mask)\n- plan_009: CKA verification (ordering reversal vs RSA)\n- plan_010: LIBERO-Spatial cross-benchmark (within-architecture only, not cross-architecture)\n- plan_011: Full-layer R² scan (exit collapse source experiment)\n- plan_012: CLIP-ViT-L pretraining control (DINO > SigLIP > CLIP, language supervision unnecessary)\n- plan_013: Branch-split RSA (DinoSigLIP specific, appendix material)\n- cross_arch_r2_matrix: 3 arch × 4 suite R² exit collapse (D102 binary separation)\n- cross_arch_l1_attention: D090 base-model control\n- cross_arch_cf: CF sensitivity with incommensurability problem\n- three_tier_gradient: N=1 at Tier-2\n- nlp_finetuning_control: D100 (ΔR²=0.000, excludes generic fine-tuning but doesn't elevate finding)\n- cross_instruction_classification: 10-way on 4096-dim (trivially easy)\n- head_ablation_suite: Specificity ratio 1.08×, ΔMSE≈0, no functional specificity\n- cf_detailed_analysis: Token overlap Spearman ρ=1.0, surface-level sensitivity\n\n## Key Tables from Paper:\n- Table 1: Cross-instruction classification — trained 99.6%/100%, random-init 100%/82%, image-mean 10%\n- Table 2: 2×2 factorial — all RSA 0.480-0.489, training effect Δ=0.003, instruction effect Δ=0.004\n- Table 5: Metric ordering reversal — RSA (SigLIP>Trained>Untrained>DINO) vs CKA (Untrained>Trained>SigLIP>DINO)\n- Table 7: R² profiles — VLA trained peak 0.678(L13), exit 0.422(L32), Δ=0.256; OXE untrained 0.609(L32), Δ=0.000\n- Table 8: NLP control — all 3 models ΔR²=0.000, flat 0.155\n- Table 10: Cross-arch exit collapse matrix — 6/6 VLM→VLA yes, 0/4 VLA→VLA no\n- Table 12: CF sensitivity — 5/7 pairs incommensurable\n- Table 14: Token overlap ρ=1.0 with Cohen's d\n- Table 15: Head ablation — specificity ratio 1.08×, ΔMSE=-0.001 (p=0.52)\n- Table 16: L1 heads — training Δ is 0 or negative across all architectures\n- Table 17: Post-D090 contribution audit\n- Table 19: Self-predicted reviewer scores: R1=4, R2=6, R3=4, mean=4.67\n\n## Your Task as R1 (Methods + Experiments)\nWrite a detailed review focusing on:\n1. **Experimental methodology**: Is the factorial design sound? Are controls adequate?\n2. **Statistical rigor**: Are comparisons fair? Bootstrap CIs, cross-validation, etc.\n3. **Experiment coverage vs design**: Which experiments from the design are covered and how well? Any critical gaps?\n4. **Reproducibility**: Are methods described well enough?\n5. **Key methodological weaknesses**: Incommensurable metrics (5/7 CF pairs), metric dependence (CKA reversal), ΔMSE≈0 implications, head ablation specificity ratio 1.08×\n6. **Missing behavioral validation**: No closed-loop evaluation at a robotics venue\n\nProvide:\n- Summary (2-3 sentences)\n- Strengths (bulleted)\n- Weaknesses (bulleted, detailed)\n- Questions for authors (3-5)\n- Scores: Soundness (1-4), Contribution (1-4), Overall (1-10), Confidence (1-5)\n- Recommendation: Strong Reject / Reject / Borderline / Weak Accept / Accept / Strong Accept\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01EShKLG3tA1TJXTqiXRAZYQ","session_id":"a551ef02-7e02-4516-a695-4e220ef1b867","uuid":"9f7e025f-a065-4e2b-b516-a64708137cc9","timestamp":"2026-05