{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_018a7HehqGz1pyVxzx2Cg7Md","type":"tool_result","content":"{\"result\":\"{\\\"success\\\": true, \\\"data\\\": {\\\"path\\\": \\\"/home/ubuntu/.agent-ml-research-idea_gen_0509_15/projects/vla-ssd/writing_plan.yaml\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"meta:\\\\n  venue: CoRL 2026\\\\n  track: main\\\\n  template: templates/latex/corl2026/\\\\n  template_note: \\\\\\\"existing paper uses corl_2026.sty\\\\\\\"\\\\n  page_limit: 8\\\\n  abstract_ddl: 2026-05-26\\\\n  paper_ddl: 2026-05-29\\\\n  title: \\\\\\\"Three Architectures, One Routing Pattern: How VLA Fine-Tuning Reshapes Instruction Flow\\\\\\\"\\\\n  core_claim: >\\\\n    VLA fine-tuning produces consistent routing reorganization across two VLM-to-VLA\\\\n    transitions (TracVLA/Phi-3, NORA/Qwen2.5-VL)—R² exit collapse (6/6 cells, sign test\\\\n    p=0.016) and counterfactual sensitivity (Cohen's d ≥ 0.45) emerge at the VLM→VLA\\\\n    transition, while L1 head counts reflect base-model priors. OpenVLA partially confirms\\\\n    (2/4 suites for R² collapse). Metric incomparability precludes cross-metric amplification ratios.\\\\n  created_at: 2026-05-22T12:00:00Z\\\\n  approved: 2026-05-22\\\\n  approved_title: \\\\\\\"Three Architectures, One Routing Pattern: How VLA Fine-Tuning Reshapes Instruction Flow\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n# ============================================================\\\\n# FLOAT BUDGET (Director-approved: max 4 fig + 3 tab = 7 floats)\\\\n# ============================================================\\\\nfloat_budget:\\\\n  main_figures: 4\\\\n  main_tables: 3\\\\n  total: 7\\\\n  appendix: \\\\\\\"dose-response, per-layer RSA, and excess tables\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n# ============================================================\\\\n# STORY ARC (D095 Cross-Architecture Upgrade)\\\\n# ============================================================\\\\nstory_arc:\\\\n  hook: >\\\\n    VLAs fine-tune LLMs on robot demonstrations, but do the internal mechanisms\\\\n    they learn generalize across architectures—or are they artifacts of a specific backbone?\\\\n  gap: >\\\\n    Prior behavioral studies (Grant 2026, Haon 2025) revealed visual dominance and\\\\n    sparse directions in single VLAs, but no work has tested whether instruction routing\\\\n    mechanisms are architecture-specific or universal, nor decomposed what training creates\\\\n    vs what it inherits from the base model.\\\\n  insight: >\\\\n    Two training effects are consistent across two VLM-to-VLA transitions (R² exit collapse,\\\\n    counterfactual sensitivity), while L1 head count is base-model-dependent. Exit collapse\\\\n    marks the VLM→VLA transition (6/6) but not VLA→VLA (1/3). Three-tier gradient\\\\n    is an observational synthesis (n=1 at Tier 2), discussed but not a main contribution.\\\\n  evidence: >\\\\n    R² exit collapse: trained Δ=0.12-0.69 vs untrained Δ=0.01-0.08 (6/6 VLM→VLA, sign test p=0.016).\\\\n    CF sensitivity: all trained Cohen's d ≥ 0.45; metric incomparability prevents trained/untrained ratios.\\\\n\\\\n# ============================================================\\\\n# SECTIONS\\\\n# ============================================================\\\\npaper_outline:\\\\n\\\\n  - section: abstract\\\\n    word_budget: 200\\\\n    priority: HIGHEST  # DDL May 26, 4 days\\\\n    core_bullets:\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Problem: VLAs fine-tune LLMs for robot control, but whether learned routing mechanisms generalize across architectures is unknown\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Method: systematic token-level analysis of 3 VLA architectures (Llama-2-7B, Phi-3-mini, Qwen2.5-VL-3B) × 4 LIBERO suites (10 cells)\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Finding 1: R² exit collapse at VLM→VLA transition (6/6 cells, sign test p=0.016) but not VLA→VLA (1/3)\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Finding 2: consistent CF sensitivity (Cohen's d ≥ 0.45); metric incomparability prevents trained/untrained ratios\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Finding 3 (base-model-dependent): L1 head count reflects pretraining, NOT VLA training\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Implication: training-induced vs inherited routing distinction, consistent across two VLM→VLA architectures\\\\\\\"\\\\n    dependencies: [experiments, method]\\\\n\\\\n  - section: introduction\\\\n    word_budget: 1100\\\\n    core_bullets:\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Hook: VLAs achieve manipulation by fine-tuning LLMs, but are the mechanisms universal or architecture-specific?\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Gap: all prior mechanistic VLA analyses on single architectures\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Approach: 3 architectures × 4 task suites (10 cells); trained vs untrained × token type\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Contributions: (C1) empirical cross-architecture analysis framework; (C2) R² exit collapse as VLM→VLA transition marker; (C3) training-induced vs inherited routing decomposition\\\\\\\"\\\\n    dependencies: [experiments]\\\\n    figures: [fig1_teaser]\\\\n\\\\n  - section: related_work\\\\n    word_budget: 600\\\\n    core_bullets:\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"VLA models + conditioning\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Mechanistic interpretability in transformers\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Behavioral/mechanistic VLA analysis → we add cross-architecture validation\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Token-level specialization\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"RSA/probing methodology\\\\\\\"\\\\n    dependencies: [introduction]\\\\n    note: \\\\\\\"mostly preserved; add cross-arch positioning\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n  - section: method\\\\n    word_budget: 1000\\\\n    core_bullets:\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"3 architectures: OpenVLA/Llama-2-7B, TraceVLA/Phi-3-mini, NORA/Qwen2.5-VL-3B\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"4 LIBERO suites: Goal, Spatial, Object, Long\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Trained vs untrained conditions (asymmetric: OpenVLA untrained=OXE-pretrained VLA, others=pure VLM)\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Analyses: probe, attention, R², counterfactual\\\\\\\"\\\\n    dependencies: []\\\\n    tables: [tab_arch_overview]\\\\n\\\\n  - section: experiments\\\\n    word_budget: 2800\\\\n    core_bullets:\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"4.1 OpenVLA deep dive (L1 routing, probe, attention, counterfactual)\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"4.2 Cross-arch R² exit collapse (6/6 VLM→VLA, 1/3 VLA→VLA, sign test p=0.016)\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"4.3 Cross-arch CF sensitivity (all trained d≥0.45; metric incomparability prevents ratios)\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"4.4 L1 heads = base-model-dependent\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"4.5 Synthesis: training-induced vs inherited routing (brief, defers three-tier to Discussion)\\\\\\\"\\\\n    dependencies: []\\\\n    tables: [tab_cross_arch_matrix, tab_counterfactual]\\\\n    figures: [fig_r2_collapse, fig_cross_arch_l1]\\\\n    d097_note: \\\\\\\"fig_three_tier moved to Discussion or removed; three-tier demoted to observation\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n  - section: discussion\\\\n    word_budget: 500\\\\n    core_bullets:\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Routing consistency across two VLM→VLA transitions = compatible with task-structure constraint (not architecture-specific)\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Training-induced vs inherited routing decomposition\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Three-tier gradient as observational synthesis (n=1 at Tier 2, not a main contribution)\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"OpenVLA partial confirmation tempers generality\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Metric incomparability limitation for CF trained/untrained comparison\\\\\\\"\\\\n    dependencies: [experiments]\\\\n    d097_note: \\\\\\\"receives three-tier gradient content from experiments §4.6 (demoted)\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n  - section: limitations\\\\n    word_budget: 200\\\\n    dependencies: [experiments]\\\\n\\\\n  - section: conclusion\\\\n    word_budget: 200\\\\n    dependencies: [experiments, discussion]\\\\n\\\\n# ============================================================\\\\n# VISUALIZATION PLAN (4 main figures, rest → appendix)\\\\n# ============================================================\\\\nvisualization_plan:\\\\n\\\\n  - fig_id: fig1_teaser\\\\n    type: conceptual\\\\n    tool: matplotlib\\\\n    description: \\\\\\\"3 arch × 4 suite matrix overview with key findings\\\\\\\"\\\\n    narrative_intent: \\\\\\\"R² exit collapse and CF sensitivity are consistent across all architectures\\\\\\\"\\\\n    design_notes:\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Heatmap matrix with Δ values color-coded\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Annotate OpenVLA Long outlier\\\\\\\"\\\\n    placement: introduction\\\\n    aspect_ratio: \\\\\\\"16:9\\\\\\\"\\\\n    data_source: \\\\\\\"artifacts/matrix_summary_table.md\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n  - fig_id: fig_r2_collapse\\\\n    type: statistical\\\\n    tool: matplotlib\\\\n    description: \\\\\\\"R² per-layer curves: 3 architectures, trained vs untrained, showing exit collapse\\\\\\\"\\\\n    narrative_intent: \\\\\\\"Trained VLAs universally show R² exit collapse regardless of backbone\\\\\\\"\\\\n    design_notes:\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"3-panel (one per arch) or overlaid\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Solid=trained, dashed=untrained\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Annotate Δ per arch\\\\\\\"\\\\n    placement: experiments\\\\n    aspect_ratio: \\\\\\\"16:6\\\\\\\"\\\\n    data_source: \\\\\\\"registry: tracvla_goal_v1, nora_goal_pipeline_v3, object_pipeline_ridge_v2\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n  - fig_id: fig_cross_arch_l1\\\\n    type: statistical\\\\n    tool: matplotlib\\\\n    description: \\\\\\\"L1 instruction-dominant head count: trained vs untrained per architecture\\\\\\\"\\\\n    narrative_intent: \\\\\\\"L1 head count is inherited from base model, not created by VLA training\\\\\\\"\\\\n    design_notes:\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Grouped bars per architecture\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Show training direction arrows\\\\\\\"\\\\n    placement: experiments\\\\n    aspect_ratio: \\\\\\\"4:3\\\\\\\"\\\\n    data_source: \\\\\\\"artifacts/matrix_summary_table.md\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n  - fig_id: fig_three_tier\\\\n    type: statistical\\\\n    tool: matplotlib\\\\n    description: \\\\\\\"Three-tier routing gradient: VLM base → OXE-pretrained → task-finetuned\\\\\\\"\\\\n    narrative_intent: \\\\\\\"Routing emerges at VLM→VLA transition and reshapes with task specialization\\\\\\\"\\\\n    design_notes:\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Radar or grouped comparison showing CF sensitivity + R² collapse + L1 heads\\\\\\\"\\\\n      - \\\\\\\"Three tiers clearly separated\\\\\\\"\\\\n    placement: experiments\\\\n    aspect_ratio: \\\\\\\"4:3\\\\\\\"\\\\n    data_source: \\\\\\\"artifacts/matrix_summary_table.md\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n  # Appendix figures (moved from main):\\\\n  - fig_id: fig_dose_response_appendix\\\\n    type: statistical\\\\n    tool: matplotlib\\\\n    description: \\\\\\\"Dose-response ablation (moved to appendix)\\\\\\\"\\\\n    placement: appendix\\\\n    data_source: \\\\\\\"registry: dose_response_curve\\\\\\\"\\\\n    note: \\\\\\\"existing figure, moved from main\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n  - fig_id: fig_layer_curves_appendix\\\\n    type: statistical\\\\n    tool: matplotlib\\\\n    description: \\\\\\\"Per-layer RSA curves OpenVLA (moved to appendix)\\\\\\\"\\\\n    placement: appendix\\\\n    data_source: \\\\\\\"registry: d041_method_b_rsa\\\\\\\"\\\\n    note: \\\\\\\"existing figure, moved from main\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n# ============================================================\\\\n# TABLE PLAN (3 main tables, rest → appendix)\\\\n# ============================================================\\\\ntable_plan:\\\\n\\\\n  - table_id: tab_arch_overview\\\\n    caption: \\\\\\\"Three VLA architectures analyzed.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    placement: method\\\\n    type: configuration\\\\n    columns: [Architecture, Backbone, Layers, Attention, Vision Encoder, Training Data]\\\\n    data_source: \\\\\\\"manual\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n  - table_id: tab_cross_arch_matrix\\\\n    caption: \\\\\\\"Cross-architecture R² exit collapse and CF sensitivity. Trained Δ >> untrained Δ in 9/10 cells.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    placement: experiments\\\\n    type: comparison\\\\n    columns: [Arch, Suite, \\\\\\\"Trained R² Δ\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"Untrained R² Δ\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"Trained CF (top d)\\\\\\\", \\\\\\\"Untrained CF\\\\\\\"]\\\\n    data_source: \\\\\\\"artifacts/matrix_summary_table.md\\\\\\\"\\\\n    notes: \\\\\\\"merged R² + CF table per Director instruction\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n  - table_id: tab_counterfactual\\\\n    caption: \\\\\\\"Counterfactual condition ranking across architectures and suites.\\\\\\\"\\\\n    placement: experiments\\\\n    type: statistics\\\\n    columns: [Arch, Suite, 1st, 2nd, 3rd, 4th]\\\\n    data_source: \\\\\\\"artifacts/matrix_summary_table.md\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n# ============================================================\\\\n# WRITING ORDER (Abstract first — DDL May 26)\\\\n# ============================================================\\\\nwriting_order:\\\\n  - section: abstract\\\\n    reason: \\\\\\\"DDL May 26 — must be finalized within 2-3 days\\\\\\\"\\\\n    deadline: 2026-05-25\\\\n  - section: experiments\\\\n    reason: \\\\\\\"Evidence-first: cross-arch sections are the core new content\\\\\\\"\\\\n  - section: method\\\\n    reason: \\\\\\\"Formalize cross-architecture experimental design\\\\\\\"\\\\n  - section: introduction\\\\n    reason: \\\\\\\"Story arc clear after experiments + method\\\\\\\"\\\\n  - section: discussion\\\\n    reason: \\\\\\\"Synthesize cross-architecture implications\\\\\\\"\\\\n  - section: related_work\\\\n    reason: \\\\\\\"Position; mostly preserved\\\\\\\"\\\\n  - section: conclusion\\\\n    reason: \\\\\\\"Compress the story\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n# ============================================================\\\\n# LITERATURE STRATEGY\\\\n# ============================================================\\\\nliterature_strategy:\\\\n  citation_budget: 35\\\\n  verify_refs: true\\\\n  micro_clusters:\\\\n    - cluster_name: \\\\\\\"VLA Models\\\\\\\"\\\\n      must_cite:\\\\n        - \\\\\\\"Brohan et al. 2023 RT-2\\\\\\\"\\\\n        - \\\\\\\"Kim et al. 2024 OpenVLA\\\\\\\"\\\\n        - \\\\\\\"Zheng et al. 2024 TraceVLA\\\\\\\"\\\\n        - \\\\\\\"Black et al. 2024 Pi0\\\\\\\"\\\\n      target_count: 6\\\\n    - cluster_name: \\\\\\\"VLA Analysis\\\\\\\"\\\\n      must_cite:\\\\n        - \\\\\\\"Grant et al. 2026\\\\\\\"\\\\n        - \\\\\\\"Haon et al. 2025\\\\\\\"\\\\n        - \\\\\\\"Swann et al. 2026\\\\\\\"\\\\n        - \\\\\\\"Fang 2025\\\\\\\"\\\\n      target_count: 6\\\\n    - cluster_name: \\\\\\\"Mechanistic Interpretability\\\\\\\"\\\\n      must_cite:\\\\n        - \\\\\\\"Elhage et al. 2021\\\\\\\"\\\\n        - \\\\\\\"Olsson et al. 2022\\\\\\\"\\\\n        - \\\\\\\"Michel et al. 2019\\\\\\\"\\\\n      target_count: 5\\\\n    - cluster_name: \\\\\\\"RSA/Probing\\\\\\\"\\\\n      must_cite:\\\\n        - \\\\\\\"Kriegeskorte et al. 2008\\\\\\\"\\\\n        - \\\\\\\"Kornblith et al. 2019\\\\\\\"\\\\n      target_count: 3\\\\n\\\\n# ============================================================\\\\n# PENDING EXPERIMENTS\\\\n# ============================================================\\\\npending:\\\\n  - exp_id: openvla_goal_standardized_v1\\\\n    status: RUNNING\\\\n    impact: \\\\\\\"fills Goal cell; write with placeholder\\\\\\\"\\\\n  - exp_id: openvla_spatial_standardized_v1\\\\n    status: RUNNING\\\\n    impact: \\\\\\\"fills Spatial cell; write with placeholder\\\\\\\"\\\\n  - exp_id: cf_batch_missing_v1\\\\n    status: ANALYZING\\\\n    impact: \\\\\\\"completes untrained CF columns\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\", \\\"total_chars\\\": 12542, \\\"truncated\\\": false}, \\\"error\\\": null, \\\"metadata\\\": {}}\"}"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01EShKLG3tA1TJXTqiXRAZYQ","session_id":"a551ef02-7e02-4516-a695-4e220ef1b867","uuid":"ab26d859-6057-4474-8346-2579f35f6f42","timestamp":"2026-05-27T03:34:51.818Z"}
