{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01UrtsKEy5VpLtXDiJjQgKiP","type":"tool_result","content":"1248\t\\centering\n1249\t\\caption{\\textbf{Structural diversity between the two VLM-to-VLA transitions.} The two architectures differ on nearly every major design axis, strengthening the generality of shared findings.}\n1250\t\\label{tab:arch_diversity}\n1251\t\\small\n1252\t\\begin{tabular}{@{}lll@{}}\n1253\t\\toprule\n1254\tDesign Axis & TracVLA & NORA \\\\\n1255\t\\midrule\n1256\tLanguage backbone & Phi-3-mini (3.8B) & Qwen2.5-VL (3B) \\\\\n1257\tBackbone family & Microsoft & Alibaba \\\\\n1258\tAttention mechanism & Multi-Head Attention & Grouped-Query Attention \\\\\n1259\tNumber of layers & 32 & 36 \\\\\n1260\tVision encoder & SigLIP (shared w/ base) & Native ViT (dynamic resolution) \\\\\n1261\tVision integration & Projector (late fusion) & Token concatenation (native) \\\\\n1262\tPretraining data & English-centric web & Multilingual web + code \\\\\n1263\tAction head design & Linear projection & MLP \\\\\n1264\tTraining data & OXE + LIBERO & OXE + LIBERO + custom \\\\\n1265\t\\bottomrule\n1266\t\\end{tabular}\n1267\t\\end{table}\n1268\t\n1269\tDespite these differences, both transitions exhibit the same exit-collapse pattern ($\\Delta R^2 = 0.156$--$0.455$), while their respective reference VLMs show only small fluctuations ($\\Delta R^2 \\leq 0.097$).\n1270\tThe probability of observing consistent collapse in two structurally divergent architectures under a null hypothesis of random association is low (permutation test $p = 0.008$; \\S\\ref{sec:delta_r2_threshold}).\n1271\tStructural diversity thus provides evidential weight beyond what the raw $N = 2$ count suggests.\n1272\t\n1273\t\\subsection{Convergent Evidence Summary}\n1274\tThree methodologically distinct approaches triangulate instruction routing in VLAs.\n1275\tTable~\\ref{tab:convergent_evidence} summarizes what each method measures, its key finding, evidence type, and acknowledged limitation.\n1276\t\n1277\t\\begin{table}[h]\n1278\t\\centering\n1279\t\\caption{\\textbf{Convergent evidence across three analytical methods.} Each method addresses a different aspect of instruction routing; no single method is sufficient alone, but their convergence strengthens the overall characterization.}\n1280\t\\label{tab:convergent_evidence}\n1281\t\\scriptsize\n1282\t\\setlength{\\tabcolsep}{3pt}\n1283\t\\begin{tabular}{@{}p{2.0cm}p{2.8cm}p{3.2cm}p{1.8cm}p{2.8cm}@{}}\n1284\t\\toprule\n1285\tMethod & What it measures & Key finding & Evidence type & Limitation \\\\\n1286\t\\midrule\n1287\tLayer-wise probing (\\S\\ref{sec:r2_collapse}) & Where action-relevant information is decodable & VLM-to-VLA: peak-to-exit collapse ($\\Delta R^2 = 0.16$--$0.46$); VLA-to-VLA: flat & Correlational (decodability) & Does not establish causal necessity \\\\\n1288\t\\addlinespace\n1289\tCounterfactual perturbation (\\S\\ref{sec:cf_sensitivity}) & Whether instruction content affects model outputs & All trained VLAs: graded divergence ($d = 0.45$--$1.52$) ordered by semantic distance & Behavioral (input--output) & Does not localize which layers are responsible \\\\\n1290\t\\addlinespace\n1291\tAttention head ablation (Appendix~\\ref{sec:action_trajectory}) & Whether identified structures carry functional signals & Dose-response: monotonic divergence ($d = 0.48$--$0.64$) upon progressive head removal & Interventional (causal contribution) & Single architecture (OpenVLA); contribution $\\neq$ necessity \\\\\n1292\t\\bottomrule\n1293\t\\end{tabular}\n1294\t\\end{table}\n1295\t\n1296\tThe three methods form a complementary chain: probing identifies \\emph{where} instruction information concentrates across layers, perturbation confirms \\emph{whether} instruction content functionally affects behavior, and ablation demonstrates \\emph{that} the identified attention structures carry relevant signals.\n1297\tNo method alone supports causal claims about instruction routing mechanisms; their convergence provides stronger evidence than any single approach.\n1298\t\n1299\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01EShKLG3tA1TJXTqiXRAZYQ","session_id":"a551ef02-7e02-4516-a695-4e220ef1b867","uuid":"474c6e3b-18b6-4972-81dc-730fefca6325","timestamp":"2026-05-27T03:34:56.699Z"}
